{%- comment -%}
  Prints ` is-active` when the given URL is the page being served, and nothing
  otherwise. Meant to be called from inside a class attribute:

    <a class="masthead__link{% render 'bf-nav-active', url: link.url %}" …>

  Accepts:
    url  - the href being tested. Required; a blank one is never active.
    link - the linklist entry, when there is one. Optional, and only used for
           `link.active`, which covers an entry whose nested CHILD is the page.

  WHY THIS IS NOT JUST `link.current`. Exact URL equality marks "Shop" on
  /collections and then drops it the moment the visitor opens /collections/all
  or a product — a nav that goes dark on the first click reads as "you have left
  this section", which is the opposite of what a marker is for. `link.active`
  only widens the test to a menu entry's own children, and a collection is not a
  child of the Shop link in Navigation. So the third test: the request path sits
  UNDER the link's.

  Appending the slash before comparing is what keeps that honest — a bare
  `contains` would mark a /pages/about entry while serving /pages/about-us, and
  every /account link while serving /account-deleted. `/` is excluded from the
  prefix test for the obvious reason: every path is under it.

  ONE TEST, THREE NAVIGATIONS. The header, the mobile drawer and the footer all
  render the same menus, so they cannot each decide separately what "you are
  here" means — the drawer is the header at a different width, and the footer
  repeats the policy menu the legal index also draws.

  DERIVED, NEVER STORED, the same argument as bf-legal-index.liquid: there is no
  setting to go stale when a page is renamed, and it survives the AJAX swap for
  free because bf-page-transition.js re-renders the header and footer groups
  from the server rather than moving a class around on the client.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign target = url | default: ''
  assign active = false

  if link != blank and link.active
    assign active = true
  elsif target != blank
    if request.path == target
      assign active = true
    elsif target != '/'
      assign under = target | append: '/'
      if request.path contains under
        assign active = true
      endif
    endif
  endif

  if active
    echo ' is-active'
  endif
-%}
